{
  "comment": [
    "What each host supports, as the source for the Platform support page on the",
    "website. scripts/check_support.js renders website/docs/support.mdx from this",
    "and checks what it can: every status is legal, anything short of `yes` says",
    "why and points at a backlog file that exists, and -- for a row that names a",
    "C++ prop -- each host's sources are grepped for it, so a box ticked without",
    "an implementation and an implementation without the box both fail.",
    "",
    "A grep is not a proof and the file says so on the page: what proves a prop",
    "`reads` overrides what counts as evidence for a row whose prop is read",
    "indirectly -- borderRadii through resolveBorderMetrics, boxShadow through",
    "core's allShadows, transform through resolveTransform.",
    "behaves is the scenario in scripts/integration_test.py, which runs on every",
    "host. This is the index, not the evidence.",
    "",
    "Statuses:",
    "  yes       the host implements it",
    "  partial   the host implements some of it; `why` says which part is missing",
    "  no        the host does not; `why` says where that is written down",
    "  upstream  ReactCommon consumes it, so no host reads it and none should",
    "  ignored   deliberately not implemented on any host; `why` says why"
  ],
  "platforms": [
    {
      "key": "linux",
      "label": "Linux",
      "toolkit": "GTK4"
    },
    {
      "key": "macos",
      "label": "macOS",
      "toolkit": "AppKit"
    },
    {
      "key": "windows",
      "label": "Windows",
      "toolkit": "Win32"
    }
  ],
